course: dictionary
lesson: 94
title: Adaptor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An adaptor is a small device that lets you connect a plug or cable to a different kind of socket. It can also mean anything that changes a thing so it fits or works with another thing.
explain: «Plugs are different around the world, so travellers use a proper travel adaptor instead of forcing a plug in.» Here the adaptor is the small device that changes the plug so it fits the socket in another country.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: «travellers use a proper device that changes the plug so it fits» still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
explain: Safety matters too. «Forcing a plug into the wrong socket can damage it and cause an electric shock.» Never force a plug, and never plug too many things into one adaptor, because it can overheat.
fact: An adaptor is a small device that connects a plug or cable to a different kind of socket.
fact: Adaptor can also be spelled adapter, and the two spellings mean the same thing.
fact: Useful phrases include travel adaptor, plug adaptor and power adaptor.
fact: Plugs differ around the world: «The UK and Ireland use three square pins, the USA and Canada two flat pins.»
fact: Adaptors can overheat if too many devices are plugged into one, and this can start a fire.
exercise: «Plugs are different around the world, so travellers use a proper travel adaptor.» What is a travel adaptor? | A type of suitcase with wheels | A plug shaped like a cat | *A device that lets a plug fit a different socket | A tiny torch for night walks
exercise: «Do not plug too many things into one adaptor, because it can overheat.» What is the main danger? | It makes the lights brighter | It becomes too heavy to carry | It stops the phone from ringing | *It can overheat and start a fire
exercise: What is another spelling of adaptor? | adaptive | adaptation | *adapter | adopter
test: «Forcing a plug into the wrong socket can damage it and cause an electric shock.» What should a traveller use instead? | A longer wire | *A proper travel adaptor | Scissors | Wet hands
test: Which phrase names a device that changes a plug so it fits a socket? | Heater stack | Pillow charger | *Plug adaptor | Fairy lights
exam: «On holiday use a proper travel adaptor and never force a plug.» Why should travellers never force a plug? | To make it go in faster | To make the socket brighter | To save time when packing | *Because it can damage the plug and cause an electric shock
